+# Runbook: Provenance & Secrets Hardening
+
+1) KMS-backed signing
+ - Provision COSIGN KMS key: e.g. AWS KMS key with proper IAM policy that restricts sign operation to a dedicated signing principal (CI runner or signing service).
+ - Set COSIGN_KMS_URI in secure environment and use cosign sign-blob --kms "$COSIGN_KMS_URI".
+ - Configure Rekor server (or use Sigstore hosted) and set REKOR_SERVER.
+
+2) ExternalSecrets + Vault
+ - Deploy Vault (HA) and ExternalSecrets operator.
+ - Use scripts/bootstrap_vault_secret.sh to populate DB creds and any other secrets.
+ - Create SecretStore pointing to Vault (see external-secrets/secretstore-vault.yaml).
+
+3) MCP Postgres migration and backups
+ - Ensure helm/mcp values.yaml sets postgres.enabled=true and postgres.secretName references ExternalSecret target.
+ - Deploy helm/mcp and verify the mcp-db-migrate job runs to apply alembic migrations.
+ - Verify CronJob backup uploads to S3 (configure postgres.backupBucket).
+
+4) Gatekeeper / OPA
+ - Deploy Gatekeeper and load constraint templates & constraints (k8s/gatekeeper/*).
+ - Deploy OPA policy bundle as ConfigMap (k8s/gatekeeper/opa_bundle_configmap.yaml) or use OPA bundle service.
+
